#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087879 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087454 :question/id #uuid "09d09b0b-2132-59b2-9eb9-ae0748f09252" :question/math-academy-id "e-21743" :question/problem "Solve the following initial value problem using the method of integrating factors.\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + 3x^2y = 9x^2, \\qquad y(0) = 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x} + P(x)y = Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x) = 3x^2$ and $Q(x) = 9x^2.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x) = e^{x^3}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot 9{x}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\cdot y & =9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{3}}) & =9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u = x^3{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{3}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 9{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =\\int 3{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =3{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{3}} & =3{e}^{{x}^{3}}+C \\\\ y & =3+C{e}^{-{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0) = 1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3+C{e}^{-{0}^{3}} \\\\ 1 & =3+C \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny = 3 - 2e^{-x^3}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048245 :topic/math-academy-id 3770 :topic/title "Integrating Exponential Functions Using Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84c716b1-12e1-584c-a0e8-f70e89466844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085479} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4b135f-e7b1-52e4-98b6-841574f71fb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085480} {:answer/id #uuid "c6fa3cf4-3e3b-5bd9-abc1-0715b68ebf64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085481} {:answer/id #uuid "fc090ec4-b599-5fc5-ac32-5c9b976c5883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085482}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a4c16bb1-0664-5e29-99cf-d582a29f1061" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1e7012e-39ed-52b9-9d95-96083e910119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - 4e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085484} {:answer/id #uuid "adcabf4f-fde7-5d05-982b-9bb7d12516dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{4}{e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085485} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc943f9-fad2-5dd7-91c8-2d1a422cac8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3e^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085486} {:answer/id #uuid "6ae2fca2-1a66-56a2-99b7-16089b2e1046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e^{x}} - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085487} {:answer/id #uuid "795a684e-06f0-5304-a914-f1ce23a39093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{e^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085488}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8a96d149-1d03-5c69-9f3f-93f3d2996138" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085483}] :question/id #uuid "9213a6d1-eed0-504f-8fac-112369977a1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-334916" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + y = 1, y(0) =-3$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\nAn integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a439c0e0-0a9c-540d-a7be-6bc235f80d36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085510} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b331bd-e501-58e2-b570-34f6391f35ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085511} {:answer/id #uuid "a8569748-2774-5243-ad71-5f254f29d10e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085512} {:answer/id #uuid "08b14b4c-3054-5ea0-9639-677d81c320ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - e^{-x^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085513} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac78c8f-9848-5777-8151-7265c4189e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - e^{x^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085514}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3037a011-e9f1-5dab-aa7d-6ffe3d4faaec" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085509} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f03f76b8-d043-505d-8492-b243b8108a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085516} {:answer/id #uuid "03978ae7-6007-56f1-bded-7c38d20b4b66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085517} {:answer/id #uuid "102ccfd1-32b7-5263-903f-1e88f2bef7f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x^{2}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085518} {:answer/id #uuid "272829e1-df88-5dc5-b413-aa305e1b1b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085519}] :answer-field/id #uuid "af75cec9-5a94-548e-88fa-c37d26f071ef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085515}] :question/id #uuid "8d9c75e9-1ee8-5d41-904e-f9bb375cf039" :question/math-academy-id "q-335808" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n$\\frac{dy}{dx} + \\frac{x}{2} \\cdot y = x, y(0) = 1$\nSelect the correct options below. An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x) =$ {{field-1}}.\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is $y(x) =$ {{field-2}}."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088145 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "117ed42d-e3b1-523b-8f69-150942e554cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308872} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7fd74c-8a73-54ba-b5f8-00d9b9214cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310020} {:answer/id #uuid "e85590a8-371b-51ed-9363-5ee1c845dfb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310594} {:answer/id #uuid "eb8ce5eb-4f47-5650-a379-9985a81218f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb8ce5eb-4f47-5650-a379-9985a81218f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310621} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f85c8ef-b569-567a-8797-508841891ad6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dac0063-ecc2-5627-bb27-eec391f6c6f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309090} {:answer/id #uuid "81429b38-817c-58d8-ba84-9a927f701049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} {:answer/id #uuid "cadb2780-5df9-5f0a-9927-a1da1d6dd3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310373} {:answer/id #uuid "d4679384-5633-50c0-98ce-64a2bd94c291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81429b38-817c-58d8-ba84-9a927f701049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309765} :answer-field/id #uuid "f955a4ed-77cc-558d-8e88-a71d0a0707d4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311524}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bd80c89-2759-5cf8-8ba7-8fb4c49482e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-335810" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=4{x}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The first step is to write the equation in standard form,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,.\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y & =4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y) & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot 4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 4x \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & ={x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(1)=2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={1}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{1}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =1+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311624 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2217ec13-aeca-54c6-b184-b9c6f12eca21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309005} {:answer/id #uuid "278ab869-b3ab-5209-b251-49e30ed08f3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309045} {:answer/id #uuid "cb884bde-aa7d-5ea3-8269-75c1c85782d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310378} {:answer/id #uuid "e304072c-14d0-5b9a-91ef-e7c21ca3967c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb884bde-aa7d-5ea3-8269-75c1c85782d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310378} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d4b8151-a2dd-5d21-b3a8-5f1786ce72f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51d8ba46-b7ec-5aeb-9c2e-92c427b44105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309368} {:answer/id #uuid "6e835f28-6c17-5099-9e1d-5557f103db76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309601} {:answer/id #uuid "784a4e7f-4997-59d7-9dbf-2d44fdbb9535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309692} {:answer/id #uuid "88322c85-406a-50de-beb7-e95ff2a7c6e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309817} {:answer/id #uuid "f316da64-a8b2-5ef5-a90e-929545648a49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "784a4e7f-4997-59d7-9dbf-2d44fdbb9535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}x}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309692} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edac9dd-3740-53a2-adc8-4f1b9b142575" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311250}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb60ed14-2886-5407-9edd-93c36aa77da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-335811" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2y}{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}},\\,y(\\pi )=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\pi )=0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311625 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48e70df3-e69a-52ce-adaf-9d80576fc124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309306} {:answer/id #uuid "4de60ca3-08eb-5908-84e7-337d050635cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309339} {:answer/id #uuid "60127d29-07b2-5438-b25c-538c97234290" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309472} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e91b0c-4363-5464-927a-584f15d25ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310236} {:answer/id #uuid "e373d4bf-5114-5201-a0ca-5837cf70ed2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7e91b0c-4363-5464-927a-584f15d25ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}x}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310236} :answer-field/id #uuid "964f9aee-69e3-5eaf-ba62-46327eb55e3f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd4c10d-4104-533e-a7ea-701ca41dc419" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309354} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab118d1-7dd3-5f85-b172-3299a04f369d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309705} {:answer/id #uuid "976ecd48-d13c-560a-802a-8e7cf948da05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309962} {:answer/id #uuid "de8dc48e-6d1c-5472-ac5b-8b94b9419130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "976ecd48-d13c-560a-802a-8e7cf948da05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309962} :answer-field/id #uuid "fba4b49a-a123-5ea4-a04f-61aaf7f9c4c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311533}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bbe03fd-0d2c-564c-9b93-a7997b3f7696" :question/math-academy-id "q-335812" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ yx & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2C}{\\pi } \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bb9195b-384d-5b2f-bad0-6dd43e0f4b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391595} {:answer/id #uuid "f34ac63a-04a2-52a7-a90f-f8f4d8d09299" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391596} {:answer/id #uuid "2d29d24c-fd03-58f5-91b9-3629bcaeee91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391597} {:answer/id #uuid "f585add5-def6-5238-932b-3a30184083f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391598} {:answer/id #uuid "a3f4e1e7-75e7-58c7-87b8-4747684ab781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3f4e1e7-75e7-58c7-87b8-4747684ab781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391599} :answer-field/id #uuid "7806b0bb-9404-54a9-9afe-9fe5aae500c4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d49da7f-4559-53d4-88e7-a4a538e83bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} {:answer/id #uuid "185130ca-9e63-5f95-8858-fbe1360a02af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391602} {:answer/id #uuid "24752170-0362-5a79-8550-d496d2deb223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391603} {:answer/id #uuid "7644849e-bdfd-532f-b35d-2dd327bd7b3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d49da7f-4559-53d4-88e7-a4a538e83bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391601} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a5f76ae-1afb-592e-a102-26dd10e20b42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391600}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c6ef87c-1a0b-5973-8a1d-74f719874948" :question/math-academy-id "q-335806" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=2x{e}^{-x},\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2x{e}^{-x}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 2x{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}y & =2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x}) & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{x} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ y & =({x}^{2}+C){e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =({0}^{2}+C){e}^{-0} \\\\ -2 & =(0+C)\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c71556-c8bb-509e-b7b6-813b830221cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} {:answer/id #uuid "dfc0fd51-b3d5-5b60-822b-55ce1a39a048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391608} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5f9c6d-a3bd-55c8-a595-021440af2d20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-5{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391609} {:answer/id #uuid "2ff86545-6fe9-59ce-a43b-d596ae985d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391610} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e86c18-962f-5498-8cd8-fd15eaf09b4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "13c71556-c8bb-509e-b7b6-813b830221cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391607} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c53fba-addc-5347-89bc-46926b4cec8a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68eff5b7-73e9-589d-b262-8718bbf64cfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391613} {:answer/id #uuid "708406f2-8554-5163-8a8c-780da5f0a24e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391614} {:answer/id #uuid "38c2efa8-509c-59df-90e0-5ff1a247796d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} {:answer/id #uuid "878ffcb1-ce95-5b25-bcf5-982716631d15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38c2efa8-509c-59df-90e0-5ff1a247796d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391615} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0dfecd2-1e22-5e5a-aff3-e35469e93c9a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391612}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cba95378-fbb4-59fe-bb7c-3f501d3e7ee9" :question/math-academy-id "q-335829" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=8,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=8.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{4x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y) & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot 8 \\\\ {e}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{4x}\\cdot y & =8{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x}) & =8{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =8(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x})+C \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =2{e}^{4x}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-4(0)} \\\\ -1 & =2+C(1) \\\\ C & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-3{e}^{-4x}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c73a7b2-a2bf-518a-beb1-31fbbadf0c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397298} {:answer/id #uuid "d70f278f-f71b-563b-90a5-a72e4490f97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397299} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9aa96a-e438-54ed-91f2-a9cd9b89c2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397300} {:answer/id #uuid "be7b681a-d4b7-5605-ba2e-22acaaed6363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397301} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397302} :answer-field/id #uuid "40c6d291-cf90-51ae-b2e3-e5400146213f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397297} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e829349-3bd7-53b1-81eb-45b5da9870a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{12x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397304} {:answer/id #uuid "ddaeb121-e0a6-501b-9a51-af6c7d17b5d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397305} {:answer/id #uuid "831b7918-1f4b-50de-b1bd-28a0091624cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397306} {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397307} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1cc20f5-acca-5b79-8f90-bd4ac033d4c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b18cb65d-b781-5075-91bf-6c656ac3ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339145" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y=x,\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/6)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =\\int 6{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}+C \\\\ y & =6+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =6+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/12} \\\\ 5 & =6+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Integrating Factors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092217 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092059 :question/id #uuid "bc48e845-b2a7-5e30-9c73-b7d842f4090c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5383" :question/problem "The point $P$ has polar coordinates $\\left( 6,\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right).$ Find the Cartesian coordinates of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\qquad y=r\\sin\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx &= r\\cos\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{2}\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 3\n\t}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\ty &= r\\sin\\theta\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} \\right)\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\[5pt]\n\t\t &= 3\\sqrt{3}\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $\\left(3, 3\\sqrt{3}\\right).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f65d032-9acc-5fe6-b7c2-b8293576cb4c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048292 :topic/math-academy-id 935 :topic/title "Introduction to Polar Coordinates"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048465 :topic/math-academy-id 268 :topic/title "Finding Trigonometric Ratios of Special Angles Using the Unit Circle"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fie