refore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(0,-2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284681 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7d1dc9-08a0-5c97-af85-8958c4f26edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-2\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281972} {:answer/id #uuid "630c3a59-ef83-541f-b9f3-e86f0db79abb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282540} {:answer/id #uuid "6d760ce6-7b53-5b17-95f0-2a701da851f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282625} {:answer/id #uuid "6fda8237-6723-59bd-aa75-aa04c8fefcec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-2\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282646} {:answer/id #uuid "8297ba5c-921d-5ae0-bd90-2ee58b877b3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fda8237-6723-59bd-aa75-aa04c8fefcec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-2\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282646} :answer-field/id #uuid "684d27ef-fb36-5be2-9f3b-9d537878d018" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284107}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0cbc4e4b-2d27-5640-8947-f02e086abba5" :question/math-academy-id "q-17134" :question/problem "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $4,$ and that $P$ makes an angle of $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ where\n\n$$\nr=4,\\,\\theta =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nF